@packages/core/src/model/retrieval.sigil import { SigilRetrievalModel }

component SigilRetrievalMarkdown {
  goal {
    Render one compact, deterministic Markdown document from a versioned retrieval
    projection so people and coding agents can inspect a component contract and its
    direct relationships without reconstructing flat evidence.
  }

  interface {
    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      SigilRetrievalModel *RetrievalProjection* provides the sole presentation input.

      renderRetrieveMarkdown(projection) returns one Markdown document without
      changing the projection, raw *PurposeRetrievalResult*, or either fingerprint.

      The sole *document title* is the *projection purpose value*, one space, and the
      word retrieval. Each selected-role *RetrievedComponent* then renders in
      *projection order*. Its heading is the *component name*. Its
      repository-relative *declaration path* follows as a *Source line* whose text is
      Source, colon, space, then the path. Zero selected-role components omit that
      block and still render *related groups*, *Diagnostics*, and *Glossary* when
      present.

      Each *selected component* renders Goal, Interface, State, Logic, Constraints,
      Decisions, Cases, Ownership, and Links in that order when each section has
      content. Each Goal, State, Logic, Constraints, Decisions, and Cases
      Facet is one list entry whose content is that unit's *semantic text*. Each
      Interface Facet is one list entry of that unit's semantic text under
      Interface or under its *Concept heading*.

      Interface content renders under a Concept heading only when the projection
      carries that Tag identity. Ungrouped interface content remains directly
      under Interface.

      Related components render after the selected component in role order:
      *Dependencies*, *Importers*, *Cycle members*, then *Module Context*.
      Each present role uses one group heading. A missing role emits no heading.

      Each *related component* heading is the component name. Its repository-relative
      path follows as a Source line whose text is Source, colon, space, then the
      path. Its stable identity follows as an *Identity line* whose text is Identity,
      colon, space, then the identity. It then renders Goal and Interface when those
      sections have Facets. A module-context component also renders
      Constraints and Decisions when those summary sections have Facets. Goal,
      Interface, Constraints, and Decisions use emphasis labels rather than section
      headings and omit a label when that section is empty. Interface uses the same
      Concept-heading rule as the selected component. Each Goal, Interface,
      Constraints, or Decisions Facet is one list entry of that unit's
      semantic text.

      Component-owned *OwnershipLinks* render in the selected Ownership section.
      Concept-owned OwnershipLinks render only under that Concept after that
      Concept's Interface Facets. Ownership uses an advisory implements, uses, or
      tests link to its repository-relative implementation file at its one-based
      entrypoint line and column. The link has a *start location* only, never an
      *end range*, and does not promise ownership, completeness, or current
      alignment. The Ownership list entry is the relation, a Markdown link whose
      label is path colon line colon column and whose target is path hash L line,
      then an optional parenthesized symbol, then a colon, space, and the selected
      section names in projection order separated by comma space when any exist. The
      Ownership heading is omitted when no component-owned OwnershipLinks remain.

      Projection diagnostics render after related groups and before Glossary. Each
      diagnostic is one list entry using the stable human text of severity, code, and
      message without path or range. An empty diagnostic collection emits no heading.

      Glossary terms from the projection render last as one Glossary list. Each term
      is one list entry whose text is the term in strong emphasis, space, em dash,
      space, then the definition. A missing glossary emits no heading.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      Use ATX depth 1 for the document title, depth 2 for each selected component and
      for Dependencies, Importers, Cycle members, Module Context, Diagnostics, and
      Glossary, depth 3 for selected section titles and related component names, and
      depth 4 for Tag identities. A selected component heading is the component
      name. Related emphasis labels are Goal, Interface, Constraints, and Decisions
      wrapped as Markdown strong emphasis. List entries use a hyphen marker. A Links
      entry writes source identity, space, two hyphens, relation name, two hyphens,
      greater-than, space, then target identity.

      Do not emit a Goal or Interface heading under a related component. Do not emit
      a heading per glossary term.

      Render remaining selected-component graph relations as an ordered list. Each
      entry uses that same *Links grammar*. Omit *origin location*. Omit a selected-
      declaration relation. Omit the Links heading when no remaining relations exist.

      Do not render raw *EvidenceKind* labels, a *matching expansion heading*, an
      implementation-source text or range slice, a *duplicate module-index contract*,
      *empty-section placeholders*, or a separate *presentation relationship map*.
      Render a non-duplicate module-context contract under Module Context.

      Preserve projection ordering. Escape only backslash, backtick, asterisk,
      underscore, left square bracket, and right square bracket by prefixing a
      backslash. After that encoding is parsed, semantic text, locations, component
      identity, and link targets are unchanged.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ComponentFirstRetrievalMarkdown {
      Decision: Render only the component-first RetrievalProjection instead of
      grouping *raw retrieval evidence* in the CLI formatter.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown structure; excludes raw JSON retrieval,
      context Markdown compatibility, workspace rendering, and compilation reports.

      Trade-offs: Markdown depends on the maintained *projection schema*, while the
      renderer becomes small, deterministic, and independent of evidence selection.

      Design issues addressed: Raw evidence headings expose retrieval internals and
      make expansions, *module summaries*, and implementation source appear as peer
      human-facing sections.

      Consequences: Component and Concept ownership is visible directly, while raw
      evidence remains available only to consumers that need it.

      Revisit when: A *projection field* cannot express a necessary agent-facing
      retrieval decision without renderer-side semantic inference.
    }

    RelatedContractMarkdown {
      Decision: Render dependency, importer, cycle-member, and module-context
      contracts with component identity plus Goal and Interface list items, and keep
      Concept headings when the projection supplies a Tag identity. A
      module-context component also exposes its selected summary Constraints and
      Decisions.

      Scope: Governs related-component Markdown; excludes selected-component section
      depth, raw evidence kinds, and dependency-decision prose.

      Rationale: Related contracts already carry *per-unit Tag identity*. Flattening
      them hides the *Tag boundary* introduced in `interface` that agents need.

      Trade-offs: Related sections grow longer than inline joined prose, while
      readers keep the same Concept structure as the selected component.

      Discarded alternatives: Joined Goal and Interface paragraphs and omitting
      related Concept headings were rejected after per-unit evidence landed.

      Consequences: Importers and cycle members become visible without printing
      EvidenceKind labels or repeating a module-index already shown elsewhere.
    }

    GlossaryMarkdown {
      Decision: Render projection glossary entries as one trailing list without a
      heading per term.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown glossary presentation; excludes glossary
      selection policy and GlossaryFile authorship.

      Rationale: Selected terms are already scoped retrieval evidence. A flat list
      avoids repeating term text as a heading and a list item.

      Consequences: Markdown can show reviewed terminology only when the projection
      carries glossary entries.
    }

    DiagnosticMarkdown {
      Decision: Render *projection diagnostics* as one list after related groups and
      before Glossary, and omit the heading when the collection is empty.

      Scope: Governs retrieve Markdown diagnostic placement; excludes diagnostic
      selection and raw evidence diagnostic units.

      Rationale: RetrievalProjection already copies ordered diagnostics, and retrieve
      Markdown would otherwise drop failures that context Markdown reports.

      Consequences: Glossary remains last. Empty retrievals do not grow a heading.
    }
  }

  cases {
    RetrievalMarkdownProjection {
      A selected component with MarkdownOutput renders its *matching expansion prose*
      under MarkdownOutput and never emits a *selected-expansion heading*.

      A component-owned OwnershipLink renders one *file-and-position link* in the
      selected Ownership section. A Concept-owned OwnershipLink renders only under
      that Concept and does not appear again under Ownership. Ownership never renders
      implementation source text.

      A selected component with no State, Logic, Constraints, Decisions, Cases, or
      component-owned OwnershipLinks omits those headings while retaining Goal,
      Interface, and present related groups.

      Two selected-role components each receive their own name, path, and selected
      sections before related groups. A diagnostics-only projection still emits the
      purpose title and Diagnostics.

      A dependency whose interface units carry RetrievalProjection renders those
      units under that Concept heading and does not join them into one paragraph.

      A module-index summary whose component is otherwise absent renders once under
      Module Context; an already represented component does not repeat there.

      An empty Importers, Cycle members, Module Context, Diagnostics, or Glossary
      collection emits no group heading.

      A selected-declaration link does not appear under Links.

      A Concept that has OwnershipLinks and no Interface Facets still emits
      the Interface heading and that Concept heading so those OwnershipLinks have a
      parent.
    }
  }
}
